SDL3 changes the ScummVM DOS port needs: interrupt handler code locked as
one section range per file, with each handler checked to lie in its range
and every lock checked (DOS_IRQCodeLocked, DOS_IRQCodeChecked).

Base: libsdl-org/SDL 1ce4c5bc2916702e8e0f6df1f612dbd8633011da
      ("ci: update cmake warning flags of the BSDs", 2026-09-26).
Apply (git apply skips this text):
  git -C SDL3 checkout 1ce4c5bc29 && git -C SDL3 apply <this file>
Build and install where build-dos.sh looks ($SDL3_DOS, ~/opt/sdl3-dos):
  cmake -S SDL3 -B SDL3/build-dos \
    -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=SDL3/build-scripts/i586-pc-msdosdjgpp.cmake \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DSDL_SHARED=OFF -DSDL_STATIC=ON -DSDL_TESTS=OFF \
    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$HOME/opt/sdl3-dos
  cmake --build SDL3/build-dos && cmake --install SDL3/build-dos
build-dos.sh refuses an installed libSDL3.a without DOS_IRQCodeChecked.

Never add an unlock to SDL's thread stacks (DOS_DestroyThread() frees a
stack that SDL_dos_scheduler.c locked with _go32_dpmi_lock_data()):
CWSDPMI keeps no lock count (paging.c lock_memory()), so the unlock would
also unlock the pages the stack shares with its neighbours -- memory that
ScummVM locked as a whole (DOS::lockAll()), or an interrupt handler's own.

